    {
      "id": 26,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Job queue depth, wait time and runner utilisation",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus-mail"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 12,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 52
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### signal not exported yet\n\nThe panels this row would hold cannot be built today. The cluster Prometheus (`prometheus-mail`) scrapes only these jobs: `kepler`, `kube-state-metrics`, `node-bumble`, `node-honey`, `node-relay`, `node-sting`, `nut-exporter`, `prometheus`, `rspamd`. No metric name below exists in any datasource on this Grafana; none has been invented here.\n\n| Wanted signal | Metric that would carry it | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| Queued jobs awaiting a runner | `gha_assigned_jobs`, `gha_running_jobs` (ARC listener metrics) | **absent** \u2014 the ARC controller and listeners expose metrics, but no scrape job collects them |\n| Registered / busy / idle runners per scale set | `gha_desired_runners`, `gha_idle_runners`, `gha_registered_runners` | **absent** |\n| True job wait time (queued -> started) | `gha_job_startup_duration_seconds` | **absent** |\n| Job execution duration and outcome | `gha_job_execution_duration_seconds` | **absent** |\n| Per-pod memory usage vs the 16 GiB limit | `container_memory_working_set_bytes` (cAdvisor) | **absent** \u2014 no cAdvisor / kubelet-resource scrape job exists on this cluster |\n| Per-pod CPU usage | `container_cpu_usage_seconds_total` (cAdvisor) | **absent** |\n\n**What this dashboard substitutes, and how far to trust it.** Because the ARC listener metrics are unscraped, queue depth is approximated by *Pending runner pods* and job wait time by *pod start-to-Ready latency*. Those proxies only see work that has already caused a pod to be created. A job queued in GitHub that ARC has not yet scaled up for is invisible here.\n\n**Envelope headroom is declarative, not observed.** The memory panels above chart *declared limits* (kube-state-metrics) against *node-level* available memory (node_exporter). Nothing on this cluster reports how much memory an individual runner pod is actually using, so a runner approaching its 16 GiB ceiling cannot be seen before it is OOMKilled. The after-the-fact evidence is `kube_pod_container_status_last_terminated_reason{reason=\"OOMKilled\"}`, which *is* charted on the GFTB / Web Serve and Mail dashboards and would appear for runners in the waiting/terminated tables.\n\n**Closing the gap** means adding a cAdvisor (or kubelet cadvisor endpoint) scrape job and an ARC listener/controller scrape job to the cluster Prometheus. Both are substrate-side changes owned by the Tinyland overlay, not by this GFTB overlay, and both are operator-gated."
      }
    }
